; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Swinging Pendulum
; CATEGORY: Animation & Many Turtles
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     physics, simulation, SIN, animation, CLEAN
; SUMMARY:  Simulates a real pendulum with gravity, so it slows at the ends and speeds up through the middle.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A heavy bob hangs on a rod from a pin. It starts pulled to one
;   side. Each frame, gravity pulls it back toward the middle a
;   little more strongly the further out it is. The result is the
;   natural swing of a clock pendulum. A faint arc shows its path.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch it swing. Change :angle (the starting angle)
;   and :length at the bottom.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a simulation: angle, speed and acceleration updated every step
;   * the pendulum rule: acceleration = - (g / length) * sin angle
;   * a tiny bit of friction (:drag) so the swing slowly dies down
;   * placing the bob by pointing the rod with SETHEADING and FORWARD
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Start at 170 degrees. Does it still swing evenly?
;   * Make the rod shorter. Does it swing faster or slower?
;   * Set :drag to 1 for a pendulum that never stops.
; ============================================================

; DRAW.PENDULUM draws the frame, rod and bob for the current angle.
to draw.pendulum
  clean
  ; the support
  setpencolor [90 70 50] setpensize 12
  penup setxy -120 250 setheading 90 pendown forward 240
  ; the path of the bob
  setpencolor [210 210 220] setpensize 1
  penup setxy 0 250 setheading 180 - 60 pendown
  arc 120 :length
  ; the rod: from the pin, heading 180 is straight down
  setpencolor [60 60 60] setpensize 4
  penup setxy 0 250 setheading 180 - :angle pendown
  forward :length
  ; the bob at the end of the rod
  setpencolor [200 160 40] setpensize 50 dot pos
  setpencolor [250 220 120] setpensize 16 dot list xcor - 8 ycor + 8
  setpencolor [60 60 60] setpensize 12 dot [0 250]
end

; STEP.PHYSICS moves the pendulum on by one small slice of time.
to step.physics
  ; Gravity's pull along the swing depends on SIN of the angle.
  localmake "accel minus :gravity / :length * sin :angle
  make "speed (:speed + :accel) * :drag
  make "angle :angle + :speed
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [240 240 245]
make "length 360
make "angle 50
make "speed 0
make "gravity 260
make "drag 0.999
forever [
  draw.pendulum
  step.physics
  wait 1
]
